I suspect this should be it (even though I did not attend):
http://www.oracle.com/technetwork/java/jvmls2013vitek-2013524.pdf

And my own two cents:
I can't wait for the core of R to be re-written, but R (and python) has too many mutables. Without type declaration, I can't see how any compiler will get even close to C/C++/Julia.
I conjecture that rewriting it in Java without some sort of type declaration will only provide marginal performance gains.

